From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:50:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/39] Draw captions ourselves: box size, alignment, outline,
 plate

The captions source wrapped OBS's FreeType text source, which only lays
text out left-aligned from the top, and its size followed width x lines,
so a long single line at the bottom centre was impossible and resizing
meant scaling.

It now renders with Qt into a texture: the user sets the box width and
height, left/centre/right and top/middle/bottom alignment (bottom centre
by default), lines (1-6), font, colour, outline width and colour,
shadow, and an optional rounded background plate with padding. Long
sentences keep the newest words, measured with the real font.

The E2E check screenshots the source and verifies a 1920x160 box, one
centred line on the bottom padding, and left alignment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
